libalpm/dload: honour CURL_CA_BUNDLE for the CA bundle path

libcurl's CA bundle path is fixed at build time via curl's
--with-ca-bundle (here /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt). That path is
absent in a relocatable /opt/msys2-cross prefix, and never present on
macOS (Apple uses the Keychain, not /etc/ssl), so the very first TLS
download fails with "error adding trust anchors from file:
/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt".

Unlike the curl(1) command-line tool, libcurl does NOT read the
CURL_CA_BUNDLE / SSL_CERT_FILE environment variables on its own, and its
compiled-in CURLOPT_CAINFO default overrides OpenSSL's own
X509_STORE_set_default_paths env-var logic. libalpm sets no CAINFO, so
there is no way for the msys-pacman wrapper to redirect the trust store.

Read CURL_CA_BUNDLE here and feed it to CURLOPT_CAINFO when set, so the
msys-pacman wrapper (which exports CURL_CA_BUNDLE=$PREFIX/etc/ssl/certs/
ca-certificates.crt) can point libcurl at the in-prefix bundle on every
platform. No behaviour change when the variable is unset.

--- a/lib/libalpm/dload.c
+++ b/lib/libalpm/dload.c
@@ -416,6 +416,19 @@ static void curl_set_handle_opts(CURL *curl, struct dload_payload *payload)
 		curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_USERAGENT, useragent);
 	}

+	/* msys2-cross: libcurl's CA bundle path is baked in at build time
+	 * (--with-ca-bundle), which points at a fixed /etc/ssl path that does not
+	 * exist in a relocatable prefix (and never on macOS). libcurl, unlike the
+	 * curl(1) tool, ignores the CURL_CA_BUNDLE / SSL_CERT_FILE environment
+	 * variables, so honour CURL_CA_BUNDLE here by feeding it to CURLOPT_CAINFO.
+	 * This lets the msys-pacman wrapper point at the in-prefix bundle. */
+	{
+		const char *ca_bundle = getenv("CURL_CA_BUNDLE");
+		if(ca_bundle != NULL && ca_bundle[0] != '\0') {
+			curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_CAINFO, ca_bundle);
+		}
+	}
+
 	if(!payload->force && payload->mtime_existing_file) {
 		/* start from scratch, but only download if our local is out of date. */
 		curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_TIMECONDITION, CURL_TIMECOND_IFMODSINCE);
